uired. A post-promotion check without a check id is post-deploy. One sentence is one row. An outcome criterion this change can ship as a test, metric or alert is \\"deliver\\". A deliver requirement whose result is only measured outside the lane (Lighthouse, field perf, a nightly or report-only suite) is \\"verify\\":\\"out_of_band\\" with \\"evidence\\" naming the job or workflow that measures it (delivered by its instrumentation). The engine tags such quotes itself; set \\"verify\\":\\"in_lane\\" when this change can check it. List every file you will change as a deliverable; tests are always allowed.\\nFirst reviews most often find defects in:\\n- requirements: One requirement per sentence or clause, each with a deliverable and a validate (omission is the top finding).\\n- deliverables: List every changed file, tests included (scope_creep flags unnamed ones).\\n- preserve: Give each preserve row a file path; it cannot be checked without one.\\nA new default-off flag or rollout key needs an activation row: defer, bucket `owner:promote:<flag>`, why = first cohort, guard metrics, shadow evidence (an AC naming shadow/cohort/treated fails if it ships off).\\nA [type:e2e] requirement needs a validate that runs a real e2e check (repo e2e set, Playwright, live stack), not a stubbed unit test; else post-deploy.\\nA validate or repro command must not read a $TMPDIR file it did not create: each run gets a fresh TMPDIR.\\nScope is enforced by the engine: it checks the changed files against the deliverables plus typed amendments itself, so do not write a file-allowlist or denylist validate (git diff --name-only | grep); the engine drops such a validate at freeze.\\nA new dependency between workspace packages (a workspace package added to a package.json dependencies, devDependencies or peerDependencies) must be a deliverable on that package.json whose change names the package and gives the reason, citing the architecture doc where there is one; \\"the lint allows it\\" or \\"t