it-required. A post-promotion check without a check id is post-deploy. One sentence is one row. An outcome criterion this change can ship as a test, metric or alert is \\"deliver\\". A deliver requirement whose result is only measured outside the lane (Lighthouse, field perf, a nightly or report-only suite) is \\"verify\\":\\"out_of_band\\" with \\"evidence\\" naming the job or workflow that measures it (delivered by its instrumentation). The engine tags such quotes itself; set \\"verify\\":\\"in_lane\\" when this change can check it. List every file you will change as a deliverable; tests are always allowed.\\nFirst reviews most often find defects in:\\n- requirements: One requirement per sentence or clause, each with a deliverable and a validate (omission is the top finding).\\n- deliverables: List every changed file, tests included (scope_creep flags unnamed ones).\\n- preserve: Give each preserve row a file path; it cannot be checked without one.\\nA new default-off flag or rollout key needs an activation row: defer, bucket `owner:promote:<flag>`, why = first cohort, guard metrics, shadow evidence (an AC naming shadow/cohort/treated fails if it ships off).\\nA [type:e2e] requirement needs a validate that runs a real e2e check (repo e2e set, Playwright, live stack), not a stubbed unit test; else post-deploy.\\nA validate or repro command must not read a $TMPDIR file it did not create: each run gets a fresh TMPDIR.\\nScope is enforced by the engine: it checks the changed files against the deliverables plus typed amendments itself, so do not write a file-allowlist or denylist validate (git diff --name-only | grep); the engine drops such a validate at freeze.\\nA new dependency between workspace packages (a workspace package added to a package.json dependencies, devDependencies or peerDependencies) must be a deliverable on that package.json whose change names the package and gives the reason, citing the architecture doc where there is one; \\"the lint allows it\\" or \\"there is a precedent\\" is not a reason on its own. Record each non-obvious choice in \\"decisions\\" with where its justification comes from (doc, lint, precedent or spec); omit the field when none. Then stop. Finish your reply with \\"Build reads:\\", the files (with line ranges) and searches the build needs; the build opens by issuing them all in one turn.\\n\\nBlast radius: list neighbours (callers, shared modules, sibling configs) from the code graph; add `\\"regression\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"G1\\",\\"command\\":\\"\\",\\"covers\\":\\"\\"}]` (engine runs it as validate). A post-deploy row needs `local_infeasible_why` and a `check` id from .forge/post-deploy-checks.json on the base, or a deliverable adding it there. Never narrow a requirement that needs another open issue\'s code: block {\\"kind\\":\\"dependency\\",\\"issues\\":[N]}. developing or fixing the signal is never post-deploy.\\n\\nAn added route needs its production ingress rule, and a touched topology.prod_parity surface its check or parity entry, cited in .forge-lean/investigation.md. No decision may swap e2e for mocked tests without a forge-probe.\\n\\n\\"blocked\\" needs a typed \\"block\\" in .forge-lean/result.json, one of:\\n- {\\"kind\\":\\"dependency\\",\\"issues\\":[N]}: an open upstream issue must land first. The engine requeues this issue behind it.\\n- {\\"kind\\":\\"split-required\\",\\"subissues\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"\\",\\"body\\":\\"\\",\\"depends_on\\":[0],\\"files\\":[\\"<path>\\"]}],\\"size\\":{\\"files\\":N,\\"lines\\":N}}: too big for one change. The engine files the sub-issues (depends_on = indexes of earlier sub-issues; files = the files or dirs each will edit, also accepted as \\"paths\\") only when every sub-issue\'s files are disjoint from the others\' or the whole change\'s size estimate exceeds 25 files or 1500 lines; otherwise keep one lane: an ordered checklist in the contract with a validate per item. In an admitted split, siblings editing the same hub (barrel or index export list, union type, shared fixture, index doc) get its slots pre-staged in the earliest sub-issue, which the others depend on, or their own per-feature files; the engine serialises sub-issues still sharing a file.\\n- {\\"kind\\":\\"design-invalidated\\",\\"decision\\":\\"<what no longer holds>\\",'... 2686 more characters
